From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marc Lainez <marc.lainez@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 11:33:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] board: lenovo: add TB3-710F

U-Boot is packed as the kernel of an Android boot image in the boot
partition, loaded by LK at 0x80008000, and boots Linux from
extlinux.conf on userdata. The console is the framebuffer LK leaves
running.

LK boots recovery when the MT6323 RTC PDN1 recovery bit is set. U-Boot
sets it on entry and clears it right before starting Linux, so a hang
in U-Boot ends in a watchdog reset into recovery rather than a loop.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
